@NickLucche  @andylolu2  @DarkLight1337 @he-yufeng Could you please take a look at another issue when you have a chance? It is related to a performance problem in Voxtral Realtime that may cause the service to become unresponsive in some cases.

For some audio inputs, Voxtral Realtime does not generate EOS before the available audio embeddings are exhausted. The offline transcription path can then continue decoding past the valid audio boundary, falling back to zero multimodal embeddings and generating many blank tokens. In my reproduction, this caused thousands of unnecessary decode steps and increased latency from about 1.4s to 55s for the same 16-second audio input. The fix limits offline transcription generation to the available audio-aligned positions.

Would appreciate it if you could help review whether this approach looks reasonable. Thanks! Have a good one!

